              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the word for \"day\" inside \"tomorrow\" (*nāḷ*, shared with Tamil *nāḷai*)]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "the \"let's ___\" ending (-ōṇa)",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the \"let's ___\" ending (*-ōṇa*)]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What are the two pieces of nāḷe sigōṇa, and what Tamil word shares the \"day\" root? (Nāḷe \"tomorrow\" + sigu \"meet\"; Tamil nāḷai — both from nāḷ \"day.\")"
            }
